<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Panglong Conference</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Panglong Agreement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Panglong Conference was a meeting held at Panglong in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shan-state">Shan States</a> in February 1947, at which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aung-san">Aung San</a>, representing the interim Burmese government, reached agreement with Shan, Kachin and Chin leaders. The Panglong Agreement of 12 February 1947 accepted their joining a federal Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> with internal autonomy. Its promises remain central to ethnic politics in Myanmar, where 12 February is celebrated as Union Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/panglong-conference.jpg" alt="Panglong Conference" width="320" height="571" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Panglong Conference · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panglong_Agreement.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
